{
 "_comment": "Leaf distances as the server cascades them. Each shape's leaves, by x,y,z: after every level tick (checkpoints 0..ticks) the leaf's distance, and whether a tick of the leaf there is pending (*), a dot where another block is. The Java harness replays the shapes at every start (LeafDistance) and holds this to the binary; the driver's engine/vanilla.rs is held to it by leaf_traces_are_the_server_s. The first shapes fix one rule each: a leaf gets a tick when any neighbour changes and none when it is placed; its tick takes the least distance around it one further; the ticks of a level tick run as they were scheduled, all taken out first, so a leaf changed in the pass schedules a waiting neighbour again; a tick runs only while its block is at its position. Then the breaking families' shapes (saws in leaves alone on the four facings, at -48 and 256 rpm; two trees; a branch; a tree with attachments), the smallest case of #448 and a log among leaves.",
